<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67507" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήποτε</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή
			ποτε</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή κοτε</span></b>  (v. infr. <i><span class="en">
			11
		</span></i>): <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> as Adv.
			<i>never, on no account</i>, after <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς</span>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				205
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Eu.</u>
				882
			</span></i>; after <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				182
			</span></i>, etc.: c. inf., <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				977
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.</u>
				617
			</span></i>; esp. in oaths, <i>never</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀμοῦμαι, μή ποτε τῆς εὐνῆς
					ἐπιβήμεναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.133
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				275
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεκέκλετ᾽ Ἐρινῦς, μή ποτε . .
				ἐφέσσεσθαι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				455
			</span></i>; in aposiopesis, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἢ μήπορ᾽
			ἆρ᾽</span> . . <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				<u>Sam.</u>
				97
			</span></i>: in orat. obliq., <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				86
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in
			prohibition or warning, with aor.
			subj., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή ποτε καὶ σὺ . . ὀλέσσῃς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					19.81
				</span></i>
			, etc.: with inf. for imper., <i><span class="en">
				11.441
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> in later Gr.,
				<i>perhaps</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1172a33
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ge.</u>
				24.5
			</span></i>, Aristeas <i><span class="en">
				15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Epict.</u>
				3.22.80
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.106d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Pron.</u>
				18.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as Conj.,
				<i>lest ever</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰσχυνόμενοι φάτιν ἀνδρῶν . . , μή
					ποτέ τις εἴπῃσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					21.324
				</span></i>
			, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδαμὰ ἐλπίσας μή κοτε ἄρα . .
					ἐλάσῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.77
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				8.53
			</span></i>.</div>
